  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> strikes the plane <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math> at a point&nbsp;<math><mi>B</mi></math> and on reflection passes through the point <math><mi>C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> If the equation of a plane containing the incident ray and the reflected ray is <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the distance of <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> from <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0,0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi>λ</mi></math> units, then the value of&nbsp;<math><mn>13</mn><msup><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
